# mayhem/sdl-sound-kat.expected - known answers for mayhem/test.sh, one case per line:
#   <file in mayhem/sdl-sound-fuzzer/testsuite> <decoder> <format> <channels> <rate> <pcm bytes> <pcm sha256>
# <decoder> is the claiming decoder's first extension and <format> is the SDL_AudioFormat it
# reports. Every case, lossy (OGG, MP3) included, must match the PCM length and sha256 exactly.
# Generated from the pinned upstream baseline (icculus/SDL_sound 0221690) by running mayhem/test.sh
# in the unpatched commit image. The mp3_mpg321_* seed is deliberately corrupt (no decoder accepts
# it), so it is a fuzz seed only, not a case here.
